# skippedbook.
#
# OrbStack's include has to stay at the very top, before any Host block, or
# `ssh orb` and the Linux machines stop resolving - and OrbStack is what runs
# this machine's Kubernetes cluster.
#
# The IdentityAgent block at the bottom was appended by 1Password itself
# when its ssh agent integration was enabled - ~/.ssh/config is a symlink
# into this repo, so the write landed in the worktree and git status caught
# it. It is committed rather than reverted, because 1Password re-adds it on
# launch and fighting that is churn.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: this machine is driven over SSH, and the
# 1Password agent prompts for approval on its own display, which nobody can
# answer remotely. The IdentityFile block above is prompt-free and, being
# first, wins for IdentityFile; IdentityAgent applies because only the
# later block sets it. If outbound ssh from here starts failing with
# "agent refused operation", that is why.
Include ~/.orbstack/ssh/config

Host *
  AddKeysToAgent yes
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_backup

Host *
  IdentityAgent "~/Library/Group Containers/2BUA8C4S2C.com.1password/t/agent.sock"
